WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.151
In this tutorial, we will walk through how to launch your vendor profile on Reliance.

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:12.185
Your goal is simple: help customers understand who you are, what work you offer, and what proof they can trust.

00:00:12.205 --> 00:00:15.065
Start with accurate business details.

00:00:15.085 --> 00:00:20.592
These details support your dashboard, public credibility profile, and approval review.

00:00:20.612 --> 00:00:23.975
Your vendor dashboard should answer four questions.

00:00:23.995 --> 00:00:25.666
Am I visible?

00:00:25.686 --> 00:00:27.774
What can customers see?

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:30.335
What increases customer trust?

00:00:30.355 --> 00:00:32.345
What should I do next?

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:35.984
Next, complete your public credibility profile.

00:00:36.004 --> 00:00:43.484
Your business photo, bio, category, specialties, and contact details shape the first impression customers see.

00:00:43.504 --> 00:00:46.291
Then build your Services Offered menu.

00:00:46.311 --> 00:00:52.725
Think of each service as a clear menu item customers can understand before they request help from your business.

00:00:52.745 --> 00:00:56.769
Saving a service offered does not automatically make it public.

00:00:56.789 --> 00:01:02.835
Approval and publishing stay separate so Reliance can keep public information clean and trustworthy.

00:01:02.855 --> 00:01:10.114
As jobs are completed, approved service videos and customer reviews become public trust signals customers can compare.

00:01:10.134 --> 00:01:19.375
To launch well, focus on three things first: a complete profile, a clear Services Offered menu, and completed work that can become public proof.
